# Citation metadata for ARPAHLS/avatar.
# Validate: pip install cffconvert && cffconvert -i CITATION.cff -f apalike
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Also record the AVATAR version you used (Git tag or release) for reproducibility.
type: software
title: AVATAR
abstract: >-
  AVATAR is an open-source desktop companion that gives a face to AI and audio:
  VRM characters with VRMA motion and real-time lip sync in an Electron overlay
  (browser/localhost for development). It can follow cloud APIs, local LLMs, or
  everyday listening — study, video, podcasts, speech, and audiobooks — instead of
  a blank background.
version: "0.2.0"
